  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 221 AM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nFor the second half of the weekend, high temperatures will begin\nto reach the mid 90s with dewpoints creeping back into the mid\n70s. This is thanks to high pressure over the southwestern\nUnited States slowly expanding east with mid-level heights\nrising. A weak cold front will also stall over southern\nMinnesota helping low level moisture to pool (e.g., rising dewpoints).\nIt currently looks like heat products will be needed starting \nSunday and persisting into Tuesday before relief arrives. Little\nprecipitation is expected Sunday and Monday. \n\nWednesday into Thursday, the mid-level ridge begins to weaken\nwith heights falling across Missouri. Multiple rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms will be possible.",
